    {
      "id": "87f64d16-9cf8-48bf-bbe4-1542954e23b1",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 327,
      "shortId": "J34RD",
      "priority": 4,
      "shortName": "show-layer-actions",
      "title": "ShowLayer / HideLayer on-demand layers → a first native exposé",
      "status": "waiting",
      "description": "Migration step 3. `ShowLayer(id)` makes an OnDemand layer visible and active, so the base context goes dormant when it is a context switch. A keybinding maps to it like any action, so it is rebindable and reachable from mouse and RPC.\n\n## 🔴 STATE — 2026-08-12. All four items BUILT; three driven; one thing left in item 1.\n\n`prefix+Tab` opens it; Enter/Space/click choose a pane; Escape/`q`/`Ctrl+q` close it.\n\n| # | item | state |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | zoom in/out instead of the fade | ✅ built — **but its exit cannot sequence the shrink before the fade** (below) |\n| 2 | floating panes drawn | ✅ built + driven |\n| 3 | `preferred_height` respected | ✅ built; **not yet driven** with unequal stacked panes |\n| 4 | `x` / `r` / `d` delete from the map | ✅ built + driven (\"seems to work\") |\n\n### 1 — the zoom (`PaintCx::with_scale` + `effects::Zoom` + `LayerRegistry::set_zoom`)\n\nReusable, per Antonio: *\"I expect they to be reusable APIs for other components and plugins.\"* The\npaint transform scales geometry **and** font size, radius, border width, glow/shadow and clip rects;\nthe effect is a sibling of `Fade`; the layer declares it like `set_fade_out`. Any layer or plugin can\nuse all three.\n\n**Direction: it GROWS IN and shrinks away** — `[settings] overview_zoom_from`, default `0.8`. Antonio\ndrove big→small (niri's reading, 1.3 and 2.0) and rejected both: *\"it should go from smaller to big,\nthe opposite when exiting.\"* The setting spans both, so it is one number, not a code change.\n\n⚠️ **Left to do: the exit plays the fade over the shrink.** `Fade::delay` and\n`LayerRegistry::set_fade_out_after` were built for it and **reverted** — a layer is retired when the\n*fade* finishes, so delaying the fade left the cards on screen after the map had gone. Sequencing an\nexit needs a layer's lifetime to follow the **whole** exit, not the fade alone. Both APIs remain in\nthe library and are correct; nothing uses the delay.\n\n### 2, 3, 4 — what they are\n\n- **Floats** are drawn at their own rect over the strip, stacked with `Grid` (one cell, offset by a\n  margin — `docs/widgets.md` → \"Placing a widget at an app-chosen rect\"), and are **one more column\n  of cells** so the cursor reaches them. ⚠️ The strip must **stretch inside its cell**: carrying\n  `align_self(Start)` there collapsed every card to a 7px sliver.\n- **Pane heights** come from `Column::pane_sizes` (the layout's resolved answer), so a stack dragged\n  out of balance is drawn out of balance. Columns also gained a `Spacing::Sm` gap.\n- **Delete** is the card's own `on_text_input` handler dispatching `close_pane_by_id` /\n  `delete_column` / `delete_workspace` through the ActionRegistry. `x` = pane, `r` = column,\n  `d` = workspace — `r`, because `x` and `X` are the same *key* and differ only as typed text.\n  Nothing was added to `WidgetIntent` or `ActionPolicy`; the confirm arrives with the action.\n  Deleting hands the cursor to the next card in the row **first**, since afterwards the neighbour\n  cannot be found.\n\n### Five bugs it uncovered, all OUTSIDE the exposé — fixed, do not re-fix here\n\nKey **releases** were discarded by the window loop · `add_named` promoted a rebuilt layer above\nnewer ones · input and painting disagreed about which layer is in front · **`close_pane_by_id`\nsearched only the active workspace** (the real cause of \"delete does nothing in the second row\") ·\na visible layer was never rebuilt when the session changed. Each has a test or a source lint. Found\nby instrumenting the whole chain **after three speculative fixes failed** — reach for the trace\nfirst.\n\n### Settled about the map — do not \"restore fidelity\" to niri\n\nAntonio overrode niri after seeing it (2026-08-05): **centre the CARD THE CURSOR IS ON**, both axes,\nunclamped. `RevealWindow` and `Component::reveal_rect` were reverted; do not reintroduce them. No\nworkspace-name gutter. Zoom and gap come from `LayoutOptions` / `[settings]`, **never constants in\n`expose.rs`**.\n\n### The map's cursor\n\n`AppState::expose_cursor_ws` records **which row** the cursor is on, so a rebuild restores it there;\n`expose_cursor_per_ws` is still the per-workspace memory used when the map opens fresh.\n\n## ✅ DECIDED 2026-08-04 — how a plugin updates a layer it already owns\n\n**Signals — the plugin never resends the tree.** The mechanism is **P085(F003)/T360** (`58SE7`): a\n`(mount, key) → Signal<PropValue>` map on `SharedChromeState`, plus a `ViewNode` that can name a\nvalue key instead of a literal, so the realized widget binds the signal and updates **in place**. The\nprop spelling is decided: a `bindings: Map<PropName, String>` map beside `events`. Both\n`PropValue::Text(\"@key\")` and `PropValue::Binding(String)` were rejected. **Rejected with reasons:**\n*replace on update* (`update_view`) — throws the retained tree away, so caret, selection, scroll,\nfocus and `FormBindings` die with it; **do not add `update_view` to `LayerRegistry`**. *Diff and\nreconcile* — no precedent here, largest thing in the plugin path, not until something demands it.\n*Immutable layers in v1* — Antonio went to the signal model directly. Full reasoning in T360; do not\nre-ask.\n\nT327 needs a **native** exposé, which updates nothing, so nothing here is blocked by T360.\n\n## Related tasks opened by this work\n\n**T416** (surface-scoped keybindings — `prefix+/` currently lights hints on the sidebar *underneath*\nthe map) and **T417** (the layer stack becomes the surface tree), both on this phase.\n**T415** (F006/P031) — config reload is a hand-written list.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "87f64d16-9cf8-48bf-bbe4-1542954e23b1-check-001-planned-in-progress",
