    {
      "id": "dcb1fdd2-065e-4632-a80b-19c1c7835e85",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 418,
      "shortId": "4RS7J",
      "priority": 7,
      "shortName": "hovering-a-card-in-the-map-scr",
      "title": "The map's hover behaviour — the autocentring loop, the animation, and a card that is hard to click",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "**Antonio, driving, 2026-08-12 (second report, after T416 landed):** *\"the animation when hovering the cards and the autocentering behavior need deeper review because its strange. mouse hover is hard to click.\"*\n\n**First report, 2026-08-12:** *\"when there is only one workspace in the exposé, moving hover with the mouse causes the map to slide right and left to center the hovered pane, but this brings it too far from the mouse.\"*\n\n⚠️ **This is a REVIEW, not only a fix.** Three symptoms are reported and only the first has a diagnosis.\n\n| # | Symptom | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Hovering slides the map to centre the card, moving it away from the pointer | **fixed twice over — see below** |\n| 2 | The hover animation itself \"is strange\" | **undiagnosed; there may be nothing left to animate** |\n| 3 | A card is hard to click | **unconfirmed; the cause it was blamed on is gone** |\n\n# WHERE IT STANDS — 2026-08-13, after T420\n\n## 1 — fixed, and then removed at the root\n\n**The fix (landed in `4eb3136`):** the reveal follows the **keyboard**, never the pointer — `CardGrid::reveal_state()` publishes \"the cursor last moved by keyboard\", and `Row::reveal_when(signal)` gates the card's `wants_visible`. Antonio drove it: *\"now is better\"*. This stays: it is a framework rule, and any list or grid that follows its cursor has the same loop waiting.\n\n**And then T420 removed the loop's other half.** The map is now built out of shares of the window, so it always fits, so **both `ScrollRegion`s in the map are deleted**. There is nothing left that could scroll: hovering a card cannot move the map, by construction rather than by a gate.\n\n## 2 and 3 — re-drive before touching anything\n\nBoth were symptoms of a map that moved under the pointer. That map no longer moves. **Do not tune an animation or a hit-test until Antonio has driven the rebuilt surface** — that is the whole lesson of 2026-08-11 (three speculative fixes, two real defects, the app still broken until one traced run found the cause).\n\nIf either survives the rebuild, then it is a real, separate defect and gets its own diagnosis:\n\n- **the animation** — the remaining candidates are the card's own cursor highlight/scale transition (`Row`'s cursor visuals) and the layer's open/close `effects::Zoom`, since the scroll animation it was probably blamed on is gone;\n- **hard to click** — look at the press/release pairing over an animating surface (a press and release on *different* targets is not a click) and at whether the card's hit bounds track the animated position (`T400`'s open half: `bounds === what is drawn === what is clickable`, with `hit_bounds` still present).\n\n# Verification (Antonio drives — all three symptoms, on the rebuilt map)\n\nOne workspace, several columns.\n\n1. Move the mouse across the cards: **the map does not move.**\n2. Watch the motion while arrowing: it starts and settles once, and does not restart or overshoot.\n3. Click a card the pointer is resting on: it activates, first time.\n4. Arrow with `ctrl+h/l`: the cursor moves and the map stays put — nothing scrolls because nothing is off screen.\n5. Wheel over the map: nothing moves, and that is now correct rather than a regression.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "dcb1fdd2-065e-4632-a80b-19c1c7835e85-check-001-planned-in-progress",
          "date": "2026-08-12T07:03:13.738Z",
          "fromStatus": "planned",
          "toStatus": "in-progress",
          "title": "Started 2026-08-12 on Antonio's instruction, straight after T416 landed and he re-drove the exposé. It is a review of three symptoms, not one fix — see the description's table.",
          "description": "Started 2026-08-12 on Antonio's instruction, straight after T416 landed and he re-drove the exposé. It is a review of three symptoms, not one fix — see the description's table."
        }
      ],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "startedAt": "2026-08-12T07:03:13.738Z",
      "completedAt": "",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-11T22:55:42.451Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-12T22:22:39.578Z"
