    {
      "id": "03a5c4c2-9bfd-4c8a-abe2-4ab1eb2b5875",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 421,
      "shortId": "RE2LB",
      "priority": 10,
      "shortName": "the-expos-is-laggy-with-many-p",
      "title": "The exposé is laggy with many panes — moving the cursor, and opening and closing it",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "**Antonio, driving, 2026-08-12:** *\"moving between panes is laggy, likewise opening / closing the expose with such a number of items\"* — three workspaces, ~25 panes. **Still reported after the T420 rebuild** (2026-08-13): *\"slowness where there are lots of panes is still a problem. opening and moving around is laggy.\"*\n\n# MEASURED 2026-08-13 — the instrumentation pass is DONE. Read this before optimising anything.\n\nA headless harness built the real `ExposeGrid` tree and timed build / layout / paint, 20 iterations each, at three sizes. Numbers per operation:\n\n| session | build | **layout** | paint |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 27 panes (3 ws × 3 cols × 3) | 1.74 ms | **1.97 ms** | 0.22 ms |\n| 81 panes | 2.46 ms | **4.76 ms** | 0.65 ms |\n| 9 panes | 0.30 ms | 0.69 ms | 0.08 ms |\n\n**In `--release` the same numbers are 0.26 / 0.22 / 0.02 ms (27 panes) and 0.42 / 0.49 / 0.09 ms (81)** — a **9–10× difference**. `cargo run -p heca` is a **debug** build.\n\n## What the measurement RULES OUT\n\n- **A cursor move does not rebuild the layer.** `InteractionIntent::ExposeCursor` reaches `record_expose_cursor` (`app/interaction.rs:945`), which only writes `AppState`; `after_mutation_change_inner` deliberately excludes `MutationKind::Focus` from `refresh_visible_layers` (`app/mutations.rs:34`). Candidate 1 in the original list is **dead** — moving the cursor costs no rebuild.\n- **The frame loop is on demand, not continuous** (`app/lifecycle.rs:155`): a frame is requested only when something animates or changes. A map sitting still costs nothing.\n\n## What the measurement LEAVES STANDING\n\n1. **`layout_layers` rebuilds the taffy tree from scratch every frame.** `chrome/mod.rs`: `LayoutEngine::new().compute(root, …)` per visible layer, per frame, with **no dirty check** — a fresh taffy tree, not a re-compute of a kept one. This is the cost in the table, it is the only one that **scales with pane count**, and it is what Antonio's \"lots of panes\" points at. The chrome tree has a `chrome_signature` retention check (`app/render.rs:1009`); the layers have nothing equivalent.\n2. **A full-screen blur runs on every rendered frame while the map is up.** `app/render.rs:1094`: `state.blur.process(…, frost_radius * scale_factor)` whenever `layers.wants_frost()`. It does **not** scale with pane count, so it is the candidate for \"opening/closing is laggy\" specifically — an animation means every frame pays it — and on a HiDPI display it is a full-resolution Gaussian per frame.\n\n## The fix to decide — do NOT ship one without Antonio choosing\n\n**Layer layout retention.** The clean version needs a layout-dirty concept `heca-grid-ui` does not have; the cheap version gates `layout_layers` on *(the layer was rebuilt) OR (the viewport changed) OR (any node reports `needs_paint`)*. ⚠️ The gate must not use `collect_damage`, which **clears** the flags the paint pass needs. A gate that misses a case produces a silently stale layout — the exact failure class that cost 2026-08-11 — so it wants its own test: change a signal that moves something, assert the layer re-laid out.\n\n**Two cheaper things first, because they may be the whole of it:**\n\n- **Ask whether the session is running debug.** 2 ms vs 0.2 ms per frame is most of the reported difference, and it costs nothing to check.\n- **`MutationKind::Config` no longer needs to rebuild layers.** That arm exists (`app/mutations.rs:34`) because *\"the exposé resolves its zoom from the room it has when it is built\"* — under T420's shares it re-fits itself from the layout engine at any size, so a resize needs no rebuild at all. Dropping it removes the resize-storm rebuild (candidate 2) **and** a per-resize `model()` + build.\n\n# Cleanup already done here\n\nRemoved `trace_layer_geometry` (`chrome/mod.rs`) — the `expose laid out:` spine trace T420's delete list named. It existed to diagnose the fit that no longer exists.\n\n# Verification (Antonio drives)\n\nThree workspaces, ~25 panes: `ctrl+h/l` moves the cursor with no perceptible delay, and `prefix+Tab` opens and closes at the frame rate the app runs at otherwise.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "startedAt": "2026-08-13T07:58:09.891Z",
      "completedAt": "",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-12T16:12:10.071Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T08:04:23.829Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "fb73a5e4-dea9-4d86-8219-71c103ada2a5",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 422,
      "shortId": "JXNAK",
      "priority": 11,
      "shortName": "the-core-s-own-overview-mode-i",
      "title": "The core's own overview mode is dormant, and `overview_zoom` now configures nothing a user can see",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "Found while deleting the exposé's fit arithmetic (T420, 2026-08-13). **Not fixed there** — it is a deletion in `heca-core`, not a component split, and it deserves its own decision.\n\n## What exists\n\n`heca-core/src/layout/session.rs` still carries the **pre-layer overview**:\n\n- `Session::overview: OverviewState` (`session.rs:15`) with a `progress` animation and a `scale`;\n- `Session::overview_zoom()` :192 — `1.0 - (1.0 - options.overview_scale) * progress`;\n- `Session::overview_workspace_geometries()` :220 — stacks every workspace as a thumbnail, centring the active one, using `overview_scale` and `overview_gap`;\n- `Session::toggle_overview()` :177;\n- `workspace_geometries()` :204 branches on `overview.is_active()`.\n\n`workspace_geometries()` **is** live — `heca/src/app/render.rs:282`, `heca/src/mouse/hit_test.rs:46`, `heca/src/app/terminal_host.rs:1093/1126` all call it. But **nothing anywhere sets the overview active**: `grep` for `toggle_overview` / `overview.progress` / `overview.is_active` / `set_overview` outside `session.rs` returns nothing. The exposé replaced it with a layer (`chrome/expose/`), which draws its own map and never touches `Session::overview`.\n\nSo the overview branch of `workspace_geometries` is unreachable, and with it `overview_zoom()` and `overview_workspace_geometries()`.\n\n## Why it matters now\n\n`overview_zoom` is a **shipped config knob** (`config.default.toml:76`, `SettingsConfig::overview_zoom`, clamped into `LayoutOptions::overview_scale` at `heca/src/app/startup.rs:74`). Until T420 the exposé read it as the fit ceiling. It no longer does — the map is built out of shares of the window and has no scale to cap. Its only remaining reader is the dormant code above, so **a user who sets it sees nothing change**, which is worse than the knob not existing.\n\n`overview_zoom_from` is unaffected and must stay: it is the open/close **animation**, read by `LayerRegistry::set_zoom` in `chrome/expose/mod.rs::register`. `overview_gap` is unaffected: `ExposeGrid` reads it as the fraction of a screen between rows.\n\n## The decision to make\n\nEither:\n\n1. **Delete the dormant overview** — `OverviewState`, `overview_zoom()`, `overview_workspace_geometries()`, `toggle_overview()`, the `is_active()` branch in `workspace_geometries()`, `LayoutOptions::overview_scale`, `SettingsConfig::overview_zoom` and its `config.default.toml` entry. `workspace_geometries()` stays and keeps its live branch. This is the answer if the layer-based exposé is the only overview there will be — which is what P082 has been building.\n2. **Keep it** if the *content* render path is meant to zoom the real panes behind the map one day (niri does zoom the actual windows, not thumbnails of them). Then `overview_zoom` is a knob for a feature that is not wired, and it should say so in `config.default.toml` rather than reading as live.\n\n⚠️ Do not silently leave it as it is: a config knob that does nothing is a bug report waiting to happen, and AGENTS § 3 forbids leaving this kind of debt untracked.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- `workspace_geometries()` has four callers; only the **overview branch** is dead. Deleting the branch must not touch the normal one.\n- `heca-core` has tests over the overview geometry — check `heca-core/src/layout/session.rs` tests before deleting, and delete them with it rather than leaving them asserting removed behaviour.\n- `README.md` and `config.default.toml` both describe `overview_zoom` in the exposé's terms; whichever option is chosen, they must be corrected in the same change.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "startedAt": "",
      "completedAt": "",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-12T22:22:21.740Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-12T22:22:21.740Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "e42ba40f-d15b-42e4-a145-8dfc05d0643d",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 423,
      "shortId": "75493",
      "priority": 12,
      "shortName": "opening-the-expos-starts-on-th",
      "title": "Opening the exposé starts on the pane the session is focused on, not where the map was last browsed",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "**Antonio, driving the rebuilt map, 2026-08-13:** *\"when you open the expose the first time the focused pane in the exposé should be the same that is focused in the scrolling area. Currently it is not.\"*\n\n⚠️ **This reverses a recorded decision** (`register`'s own comment: *\"the remembered highlight wins because it is the more specific answer\"*). Antonio reversed it — the map is a picture of **where you are**, so it opens where you are.\n\n# FIXED 2026-08-13 — uncommitted on `feat/palette-modes`. ⏳ AWAITING ANTONIO'S DRIVE.\n\n## The defect\n\n`heca/src/chrome/expose/mod.rs`. The workspace was gated on whether the map was already up; **the pane was not** — `expose_cursor_per_ws[row]`, written by `record_expose_cursor` on every cursor move, won on a fresh open too. Open the map, arrow to another pane, dismiss, move nowhere: the next open started on the pane you browsed to while the session was still focused on the one you left, so the map drew its cursor on one card and its `active` styling on another.\n\n## The fix\n\nThe resolution is now one **pure function**, `open_on(session, already_up, cursor_ws, cursor_per_ws) -> Option<PaneId>`, because it had been got wrong three times and could not be tested where it lived:\n\n- **opening** → `session.active_workspace().active_pane()`. `active_pane()` answers for both domains — the focused float when one is active, the tiled pane otherwise — which is the same rule the model marks a card `active` by, so the cursor and the styling agree by construction;\n- **rebuilding while up** → the remembered pane in the row the cursor is in, so a rebuild never moves the highlight (deleting a pane in one row must not jump the map to another — Antonio, 2026-08-11);\n- a remembered pane that has since been **deleted** falls through to the session's focus.\n\nIt takes the `Session`, not the `AppState` around it, so all four answers are testable without a window.\n\n## Tests (4, in `chrome/expose/mod.rs`)\n\n- `opening_the_map_starts_on_the_pane_the_session_is_focused_on` — with a *different* pane remembered, and an assertion that the fixture really differs;\n- `rebuilding_the_map_keeps_the_cursor_where_it_stands`;\n- `a_rebuild_stays_in_the_row_the_cursor_is_in` — cursor in row 1 while the session is focused in row 0;\n- `a_remembered_pane_that_no_longer_exists_falls_back_to_the_session`.\n\nWorkspace green, clippy 0 warnings.\n\n# Verification (Antonio drives)\n\nFocus a pane, open the map: the cursor is on it. Arrow away, Esc, open again: the cursor is back on the focused pane, not where you browsed. Then, with the map up, delete a card in a non-active row: the map stays in that row.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\n**Verified by Antonio, 2026-08-13: *\"works great.\"***\n\nShipped as the pure `open_on(session, already_up, cursor_ws, cursor_per_ws) -> Option<PaneId>` in `heca/src/chrome/expose/mod.rs`, with four tests covering opening, rebuilding, rebuilding in a non-active row, and a remembered pane that no longer exists. Uncommitted on `feat/palette-modes`.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
