      "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T07:55:44.769Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "e21ee3b7-63a1-4e3a-a3de-b37f8e9ca032",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 425,
      "shortId": "3XV9H",
      "priority": 13,
      "shortName": "the-keyboard-cursor-gets-its-o",
      "title": "Selection and cursor differ in KIND, not hue — a filled panel inside a glowing ring",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "Found by Antonio driving the rebuilt exposé (T420), 2026-08-13: *\"make the pane border color in the exposé different from the selected pane highlight. when we hover over the focused it's not easy to understand where the current focus is.\"*\n\n# The defect\n\nTwo marks answer two different questions — **where the cursor is** versus **what is selected** — and `Row` draws them on the **same rectangle** (`Base::highlight_rect(SEL_INSET)`), the nav outline last. Both were an accent fill plus an accent edge, so the outline overwrote the active border and the two states became one exactly when they coincided. `DockFrame` had it identically (accent wash + accent ring), and **both carried a comment claiming the cursor was \"a distinct colour\"** — which the code had never done.\n\n# Two failed attempts, and why hue could never fix it\n\n1. **`foreground`** (honouring the old comment) — Antonio: *\"still not distinguishable.\"*\n2. **A dedicated amber `nav_cursor` token** — Antonio: *\"orange is not a great color for tron legacy\"*, and the same value was carried across three themes with different identities.\n\nThe reason hue cannot work, measured:\n\n| theme | foreground | accent | glow |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| grid_tron | `#c6f0ff` | `#29b4fa` | `#29b4fa` |\n| mocha | `#cdd6f4` | `#89b4fa` | `#89b4fa` |\n| latte | `#4c4f69` | `#52679f` | `#52679f` |\n\n`glow == accent` in all three and each foreground is a pale tint of it, so any borrowed token is a variation on the thing it must contrast with. Antonio's own proposal, `#012B37`, measured **1.33:1 against grid_tron's background** and 1.26:1 against its surface — a *surface* tone, invisible as a line.\n\n# The fix — decided with Antonio, 2026-08-13\n\n**They differ in KIND: selection is a FILL, the cursor is an EDGE.** A ring lets whatever is under it show through, so the cursor can sit on the selected row and both stay readable. Hue never has to carry the distinction again.\n\n- **`Theme::selected_background: Option<Color>`** replaces the amber `nav_cursor`, with `effective_selected_background()` deriving it when unset: `surface.lerp(accent, 0.18)` — built from the theme's own two colours, so a user's theme gets a coherent selection without naming one.\n- **`Row::paint`** — active draws the panel and **no border**; nav draws the accent ring + glow and **no fill** (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/row.rs`).\n- **`DockFrame::paint`** — the active wash becomes the same panel; the cursor is the accent ring (`widgets/dock_frame.rs`). One rule for the whole library, which Antonio chose over a per-widget override.\n- **The three `.highlight(theme.colors.accent)` call sites are gone** — `chrome/expose/pane_card.rs`, `providers/workspaces/mod.rs`, `examples/showcase.rs`. Forcing the accent as the highlight is what pinned the selection to the cursor's colour. `Row::highlight` survives for a genuinely state-tinted row.\n\n## Per theme, in its own idiom (Antonio: *\"latte is a light theme and mocha a dark alternative to tron\"*)\n\n| theme | selected panel | vs background | text on it | accent ring on it |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| grid_tron | `#103d52` (surface lifted toward the cyan) | 1.71 | 9.56 | 4.97 |\n| mocha | `#45475a` (Catppuccin Mocha Surface1) | 1.80 | 6.31 | 4.33 |\n| latte | `#bcc0cc` (Catppuccin Latte Surface1 — **darker** than the page, as a light theme's selection must be) | 1.61 | 4.39 | 3.04 |\n\nWorkspace green, clippy 0 warnings. Uncommitted on `feat/palette-modes`.\n\n# Verification (Antonio drives)\n\nExposé: move the cursor onto the pane that is already focused — a teal panel *inside* a neon ring, both readable. Sidebar: the same on a workspace frame and on a row. Then `prefix+Shift+r` after editing `selected_background` in a theme — it retunes without a rebuild.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "e21ee3b7-63a1-4e3a-a3de-b37f8e9ca032-check-001-planned-in-progress",
