    {
      "id": "21518dd0-4ef6-47fd-b62c-1c309001d5db",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 426,
      "shortId": "XBCDT",
      "priority": 14,
      "shortName": "show-where-back-and-forth-lead",
      "title": "Show where back-and-forth leads — a subtle mark on the last-visited pane and workspace",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "**Antonio, driving, 2026-08-13:** *\"Because we have back and forth binding last pane and last ws it would be useful to highlight the last visited pane or ws so that we know exactly where back and forth lead. A very subtle difference if possible.\"*\n\nThis is the \"different colour for selected and last selected\" he remembered — it is **not** a state that was lost; it has never been drawn. The state exists and drives real bindings; nothing surfaces it.\n\n# What already exists — do not invent a parallel notion\n\n`heca/src/app_state.rs`:\n- `last_visited_ws_idx: Option<usize>` :777 — the workspace `prefix+Shift+l` returns to.\n- `last_visited_pane_per_ws: Vec<Option<PaneId>>` :779 — per workspace, the pane `prefix+i` returns to. (Note the doc at :788 warns another field is deliberately **not** this one — read it before reusing either.)\n\nRead by `handlers.rs`: `handle_focus_toggle_local` :85 (`last_visited_pane_per_ws[active_ws]`) and `handle_focus_toggle_global` :100 (`last_visited_ws_idx`). Maintained around :1290 when a workspace is removed. **These two fields are the single source of truth for where back-and-forth leads** — the mark must read them, never re-derive a history.\n\n# What to build\n\nA **third**, deliberately faint state, one level below selection, in the existing hierarchy:\n\n| weight | means | drawn as |\n|---|---|---|\n| faint wash (`active_wash_alpha`) | the current **workspace** | `DockFrame` active |\n| **new: fainter still** | **where back-and-forth would take you** | this task |\n| opaque panel (`selected_background`) | the selected **row** | `Row` active |\n| glowing accent ring | where the **cursor** is | `Row`/`DockFrame` nav |\n\nThree pieces:\n\n1. **`heca-grid-ui`** — a `Row::previous(bool)` / `DockFrame::previous(bool)` signal-backed state (same shape as `active`, so the host flips it in place through `sync_chrome_signals` without a rebuild), painted before the active fill so selection always wins where both are true. ⚠️ It must be a **property on the widget**, not a per-caller recipe (⭐⭐ RULE ZERO), and it must not be a fourth *hue*: the lesson of T425 is that hue cannot carry a distinction on this palette. A very light wash of `selected_background` — an alpha well below `active_wash_alpha` — is the shape that fits.\n2. **`heca-theme`** — the alpha as a token beside `active_wash_alpha` (e.g. `previous_wash_alpha`), so each theme tunes how subtle \"subtle\" is. Latte will want a different value from the dark themes, as everything else has.\n3. **The app** — `providers/workspaces/mod.rs::pane_card` sets it from `last_visited_pane_per_ws[ws_idx]`, and the workspace `DockFrame` from `last_visited_ws_idx`. The exposé's `PaneCard` should carry it too: the map is where \"where would I land\" is most useful.\n\n# Edge cases\n\n- The last-visited pane is often **also** the cursor's row or the selected row. All four states must be able to stack on one row and stay separable — that is what the fill/edge split from T425 buys, and this must not spend it.\n- `last_visited_ws_idx` is `None` on a fresh session and after the target workspace is deleted (:1290). Nothing marked is the correct picture then, not a mark on index 0.\n- A workspace's remembered pane may have been closed since — check it still resolves (`app::focus::find_pane_workspace`) exactly as `chrome/expose/mod.rs::open_on` does.\n\n# Verification (Antonio drives)\n\nWith several panes: the pane `prefix+i` would return to carries a mark you can find when you look for it and never notice when you are not. Same for the workspace under `prefix+Shift+l`. Press the binding — you land on the marked one, and the mark moves to where you came from.",
